    "Id": "vehicledef_GALLEON_GAL104",
    "Name": "Galleon GAL-104",
    "Details": "A light combat vehicle that first saw production in 2692 the Galleon proved to be an economical means of supporting infantry and BattleMechs. With a top speed faster than most 'Mechs, the Galleon was mobile but generally lacked protection, early models carrying only three and a half tons of armor. After the Exodus, these tracked vehicles mostly fell into the possession of the Draconis Combine and the Free Worlds League. The Galleon is often paired with the Harasser Missile Platform.\n\n<b><color=#ffcc00>Biome Restrictions: None.</color></b>\n\n<b><color=#ffcc00>Movement: 7/11 hexes / 210/330 meters.</color></b>\n\n<color=#ffcc00><b>Armor:</b> Ferro-Fibrous\n<b>Structure:</b> Structure\n<b>Values       A        S  </b>\n<b>Front</b>       160     15\n<b>Left</b>         100     15\n<b>Right</b>       100     15\n<b>Rear</b>        100     15\n<b>Turret</b>      145     15\n\n<b>Total</b>      605     75</color>\n\n<color=#ff0000>Quirk: Protected Mechanisms</color>",
    "Icon": "Galleon"
  },
